# Line-ending policy.
#
# Windows-native tooling stays CRLF (PowerShell, MSVC project files). Source,
# docs, and cross-platform text are pinned to LF so they are deterministic and do
# not depend on core.autocrlf -- that is what ends the CRLF<->LF churn. Retained
# proof transcripts stay binary so their SHA-256 (bound by proof ledgers) never
# drifts.
#
# To end existing churn, run ONCE on a CLEAN tree:
#   git config core.autocrlf false
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git commit -m "normalize line endings; end CRLF/LF churn"
# NOTE: .dts / .csv / .txt are left as text=auto (not force-flipped) because some
# are checksum-bound or Windows-authored data; verify none are SHA-pinned before a
# full renormalize, and add a `-text` guard here for any that are.

* text=auto

# Received external-AI packages are PRESERVED VERBATIM (AIF-102). Their manifests
# claim the payload is "unchanged, exactly as rendered by the producing agent", and
# a text=auto round-trip would silently rewrite line endings and make that claim
# false. Byte-preservation is the whole point of the landing zone, so the payload
# is marked -text. Applies to the payload only; the .md manifest/assessment written
# locally beside it stay normal text.
docs/maintenance/external_ai_intake/**/received_slides/**   -text
docs/maintenance/external_ai_intake/**/payload/**           -text

# Windows scripts & MSVC project files -> CRLF (native tooling expects it)
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.sln       text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj   text eol=crlf
*.props     text eol=crlf

# Source and cross-platform text -> LF (deterministic; independent of autocrlf)
*.cpp   text eol=lf
*.cxx   text eol=lf
*.cc    text eol=lf
*.c     text eol=lf
*.hpp   text eol=lf
*.hxx   text eol=lf
*.h     text eol=lf
*.ipp   text eol=lf
*.inl   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
# MANIFEST.txt is GENERATED (tools/staging/generate_public_manifest.py, AIF-092)
# and the generator writes LF. Left at `text=auto` it materializes as CRLF on a
# Windows checkout, so every regeneration would flip it back and the file would
# read as perpetually modified. Pinned per-file, not by class: the `.txt` note
# above deliberately leaves the class alone because some are checksum-bound or
# Windows-authored. Verified 2026-08-07 that this one is neither -- it is
# referenced by nothing but its own generator and is rewritten wholesale.
MANIFEST.txt text eol=lf

# Binary files (never normalize)
*.zip   binary
*.exe   binary
*.dll   binary
*.lib   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.obj   binary
*.pyd   binary
*.dbf   binary
*.dbt   binary
*.cdx   binary
*.fpt   binary
*.inx   binary
*.mdb   binary

# Retained raw runner transcripts (e.g. teed console captures, possibly UTF-16
# with ANSI codes). Treat as binary so no CRLF/encoding normalization can drift
# the SHA-256 that proof ledgers bind (e.g. PINOCCHIO_HISTORICAL_ENGINE_BENCHMARKS).
labtalk/proofs/runs/*.log   binary
